          "The survey should also distinguish the net's orientation and purpose. A vertical exclusion panel at an accessible utility opening is a different proposal from netting across the top of a deep common shaft. Horizontal netting can collect material and requires a practical inspection and cleaning plan. Do not approve a location simply because it covers the largest visible gap; review how the space functions afterwards.",
